  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude, slice items[1338:1344]). This brick is a derived RDF transformation of the intermediate brick 'nih-pubchem-bioassays', which is the NCBI PubChem BioAssay archive. The convert.py stamps the output with the NLM download terms IRI; PubChem/NCBI government-created content is public domain and freely redistributable, including commercially, so classed open / commercial permitted (matching the repo precedent for other PubChem BioAssay bricks). The repo had no .bb/source.jsonld. HUMAN REVIEW: PubChem BioAssay aggregates depositor-submitted assays that may retain third-party rights (the README flags this explicitly); confirm before any authoritative commercial-use assertion.",
